@format 1
@id processing.source-output-collision
@title Handle source and output path collision
@area 5. Processing and FFmpeg
@entry input
@summary Reject a work item whose normalized output path equals any input path before collision handling or FFmpeg can alter the source.
@section II. Functionality
@flow TB
@related processing.run-job, queue.create-edit-work, queue.create-convert-work, queue.create-audio-work, queue.create-split-work, queue.create-merge-work
@tag collision
@tag overwrite

@alias edit = Cadroue.Application.LEdit
@alias convert = Cadroue.Application.LConvert
@alias audio = Cadroue.Application.LAudio
@alias split = Cadroue.Application.LSplit
@alias merge = Cadroue.Application.LMerge
@alias job = Cadroue.ShellEngine.LJob

[input] Work output path is formed <input>
- Avoid an exact source/output path match by appending an edit suffix for Edit work @ edit.LEditNameCreate(...)
- Avoid an exact source/output path match by appending a convert suffix for Convert work @ convert.LConvertNameCreate(...)
- Avoid an exact source/output path match by appending an audio suffix for Audio work @ audio.LAudioNameCreate(...)
- Create Split names with within-batch uniqueness but without a full-path comparison against the source @ split.LSplitNameCreate(...)
- Create Merge names with within-batch uniqueness but without comparison against every merge source @ merge.LMergeNameCreate(...)
> validate

[validate] Validate resolved input and output paths <decision>
- Normalize the final output path and compare it with every input path using Windows path semantics @ job.LJobInputCollisionCheck(...)
? "Output equals an input path" > rejected
? "Every input path is distinct" > policy

[rejected] Reject unsafe work <error>
- Stop before live registration, directory creation, collision handling, stage construction, or FFmpeg startup @ job.LJobRun(...)
- Mark the item failed, persist the reason, reload the schedule, and apply runner failure behavior @ job.LJobRun(...)
= The source remains untouched and the failed item records why it was rejected.

[policy] Apply policy only to a distinct output path <decision>
- Handle an existing destination only after validation proves it is not an input @ job.LJobCollisionApply(...)
? "Rename output" > rename-output
? "Rename existing" > rename-existing
? "Overwrite" > overwrite

[rename-output] Move output to a free path <process>
- Resolve a free output name and update the work item's output path @ job.LJobCollisionApply(...)
> normal

[rename-existing] Move the existing destination away <process>
- Resolve a free name and move the distinct existing destination @ job.LJobCollisionApply(...)
> normal

[overwrite] Replace a distinct destination <process>
- Leave the distinct output path in place for FFmpeg overwrite handling @ job.LJobCollisionApply(...)
> normal

[normal] Continue with distinct paths <output>
= FFmpeg receives separate source and output paths.
